    Validator 1.1 Copyright (c) 1999 CDI, cdi@thewebmasters.net

    6 New methods in release 1.1

    + = Modified since 1.0
    * = New since 1.0

    METHOD            DESCRIPTION                            CLASS VERSION

    // Tests

*    has_html         string has HTML specials in it              1.1

*    has_metas        strings has META chars in it                1.1

    // Manipulations
*    strip_metas      strips META chars from string               1.1

*    custom_strip     strips user defined array of chars          1.1
                      from a string and returns the results

    // Internet host and url tests
+    is_hostname       Fully qualified Hostname)                  1.1
*    is_bigfour        checks TLD for com,net,edu,org)            1.1
                       Use this with is_country() to check
                       validity of a TLD

    // Misc methods
*    browser_gen        returns the "generation" of the current  1.1
                        clients browser

            Mozilla/1                            => FIRST
            Mozilla/2 or Lynx                    => SECOND
            Mozilla/3,Opera,Konqueror,IBrowse    => THIRD
            Mozilla/4                            => FOURTH
            Mozilla/5                            => FIFTH
                                        (Yes there ARE 5.0 browsers!)

            Specials    SPAMMER       == Known SPAMMER user agent.
                        SPIDER        == Known search engine spider/robot
                        ANONYMIZER    == Anonymizer access

        If the user agent is unrecognized or undefined, browser_gen()
        returns UNKNOWN. It doesn't recognize many spiders yet, feel
        free to add as many as you want.

